  "problem": "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- $(-\\infty ,-2)$\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-\\infty ,-2)$ is open. The boundary point of the set is $-2$ and it does not lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $2$, $7$, and $9$, and the points $2$, $7$, and $9$ lies in the set.\n\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$ has four boundary points $-5$, $-1$, $2$, and $4$, and the points $-5$ and $-1$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
